<Application xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="TanMenu.Wpf.App">

  <!--
    Three style layers, in this order:

      1. FluentTheme        — the standard control set (settings window, message box): tabs,
                              dropdowns, checkboxes, text boxes, scrollbars, focus, IME. Avalonia's
                              own theme is Fluent 1 vocabulary, which layer 2 re-proportions.
      2. Fluent2/Tokens     — TanMenu's Fluent 2 design tokens, Light + Dark. Also overrides the
                              four FluentTheme keys this app redefines for Avalonia's own templates:
                              ControlCornerRadius, OverlayCornerRadius and
                              ContentControlThemeFontFamily, which pull the standard controls into
                              Fluent 2 proportions and typography, plus TitleBarBackgroundBrush,
                              which clears the opaque band Avalonia's drawn window decorations
                              otherwise paint behind MainWindow's title strip. That seam works
                              because this file is listed AFTER FluentTheme below and
                              Application.Styles is searched last-first — Tokens.axaml is the
                              authority on it and carries the measurements; do not re-derive it here.
      3. Fluent2/Launcher   — the launcher's own dialect. Every rule is an x:Key'd ControlTheme or a
                              .tm-* class selector, so it is opt-in and cannot leak into the
                              settings window or the message box.

    RequestedThemeVariant is deliberately NOT pinned here any more. The retro theme was a fixed
    light palette, so the old build had to force Light or the OS could put dark Fluent chrome around
    a light launcher. Fluent 2 has both variants, so the variant is a user setting
    (general.appearance) applied at startup by Services/AppTheme.
  -->
  <Application.Styles>
    <FluentTheme />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://TanMenu.Wpf/Themes/Fluent2/Tokens.axaml" />
    <StyleInclude Source="avares://TanMenu.Wpf/Themes/Fluent2/Launcher.axaml" />
  </Application.Styles>

</Application>
